when russia's war hit this small village  outside kiev it took the heart out of a  single road  p street  two young men grew up together here a  few houses apart  victor ballet in the yellow t-shirt  pavel koladenko in the white  now two shattered families are all  that's left  they say russian soldiers captured  tortured and shot the childhood friends  their broken bodies found buried  together in a shallow grave  the local priest the only comfort  push  foreign  she clung to the memory of her only  child  victor and pavel both used to serve in  the military it's probably why they were  murdered she last spoke to her son in  late february when russian tanks rolled  into the village  the two friends had been planning to  volunteer to fight again  much  as we spoke pavel's mother appeared  she showed us their house  and her raw paintings  [Music]  and do you believe that um your son and  his friend were  captured and tortured and killed  together  photographs of pavel remembered fondly  he and victor were only 28 years old  no one knows what day they died  their remains only found after russian  forces withdrew  the priest helped give them a proper  burial  he showed us pavel's final resting place  a permanent reminder of what russia's  war did to the two young friends from  peace street  debra haynes sky news zed  outside kiev
 

